# What NOT to upload when `gcloud builds submit` sends this directory to Cloud Build.
#
# This file exists because of a trap: when there is no `.gcloudignore`, gcloud falls back to
# `.gitignore`. That would be exactly wrong here, because `models/` is git-ignored on purpose
# and the image must contain the model. The build would succeed and the container would die
# at startup with "no model at /app/models/model.joblib".
#
# So the rule is inverted from git's: upload what the image needs, exclude what it does not.

# --- never upload: third-party data, local state, caches -------------------------------
data/raw/*
!data/raw/README.md
data/*.db
*.db
mlruns/
mlartifacts/
mlflow.db

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- never upload: secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
kaggle.json
*.pem
*.key

# --- not needed in the build context ---------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
docs/
notebooks/
design-system/
deploy/
tests/
reports/*.md
*.md
!README.md

# `models/` is deliberately NOT ignored here. The image copies the model in, and the
# container refuses to start without it.
